    },
    "message": "Stop re-reading unchanged history entries in a save's full validation\n\nThe full validation before each Checkpoint save read every append-only\nhistory again, about 130 ms of a save near day 7. A writer's history cache\nnow compares each history with the documents of its last save, in one strict\npass that tells 1 from True and a tuple from a list, and the rules read only\nthe entries after the unchanged ones; the ledger and shared operations\nreplays continue from their kept state. A changed old entry, or a change in\nwhat the rules of old entries read, reads that whole history in the same save.\n\nThe memo exists only with the kernels, starts empty for a restored world and\nis dropped by any failed capture.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
